hadiths[107]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18537","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, from Khaythamah and al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Lawful is clear, unlawful is clear, and doubtful matters are between them. Whoever leaves doubtful matters is even more likely to leave the unlawful, and the prohibitions of Allah are a sanctuary, so whoever pastures around the sanctuary is likely to pasture in it."
"18538","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, from Khaythamah and al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then there will come a people whose oaths precede their testimony and whose testimony precedes their oaths."
"18539","Hasan and Yunus said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Khaythamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of this nation are the generation among whom I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then those who follow those who follow them. Hasan said: Then there will arise peoples whose oaths precede their testimony and whose testimony precedes their oaths."
"18540","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Amir, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he raised it, he said: Part of raisins is wine, part of dates is wine, part of wheat is wine, part of barley is wine, and part of honey is wine."
"18541","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, then he mentioned a hadith, he said: And he narrated from Abu Qilabah, from a man, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he would pray two rak'ahs, then supplicate, then pray two rak'ahs, then supplicate, until the sun cleared. He said: He said: Some people of ignorance say, or claim, that when the sun and moon eclipse, one of them only eclipses for the death of a great one among the great of the people of the earth, and that is not so, but they are two creations among the creation of Allah, so when Allah Almighty manifests Himself to something of His creation, it humbles itself to Him."
"18542","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-A'mash and Mansur, from Dharr, from Yusay' al-Kindi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Supplication is worship. Then he recited: Call upon Me, I will answer you. Indeed those who are too proud for My worship."
"18543","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Awwam, he said: A man of the Ansar of the family of al-Nu'man ibn Bashir narrated to me, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us while we were in the mosque after the Isha prayer, he raised his gaze to the sky, then lowered it until we thought something had happened in the sky, then he said: Indeed there will be after me rulers who lie and oppress, so whoever believes them in their lies and supports them in their oppression is not of me, nor am I of him. And whoever does not believe them in their lies and does not support them in their oppression is of me, and I am of him. Indeed the blood of the Muslim is its expiation. Indeed: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, they are the lasting good deeds."
"18544","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that his father granted him a gift, so the mother of al-Nu'man said to him: Call my son as witness to this gift. So he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him, so he said to him: Did you give all your children what you gave this one. He said: No. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, disliked testifying for him."
"18545","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The example of the believer is like the body: when a man's head complains, the rest of his body responds to it."
"18546","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, al-Nu'man ibn Bashir narrated to us, speaking upon the pulpit of Kufah: By Allah, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or he said: Your Prophet, peace be upon him, would not eat his fill of poor-quality dates, while you are not satisfied with less than varieties of dates and butter."
"18547","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, from Simak, that he heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir delivering a sermon, saying: I praise Allah Almighty, for there would often come upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a month in which he remains writhing, not eating his fill of poor-quality dates."
"18548","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Muhammad ibn al-Nu'man ibn Bashir and Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf informed me, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: My father Bashir ibn Sa'd went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to call him to witness a gift he had granted me, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Did you grant all your sons the like of this. He said: No. He said: Then take it back."
"18549","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us, Abu al-Duha narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir say: My father took me to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, meaning to call him to witness a gift he was giving me, so he said: Do you have another child besides him. He said: Yes. He said: Then make them equal."
"18550","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Simak, he said: I heard al-Nu'man delivering a sermon, wearing a cloak of his, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, delivering a sermon, saying: I warn you of the Fire. If a man in such-and-such place heard his voice."
"18551","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The example of the one who upholds the limits of Allah Almighty and the one who compromises in them is like the example of a people who drew lots for a ship in the sea, so some of them got its lower part and some of them got its upper part, then those in its lower part would climb up and draw water and pour it upon those in its upper part, so those in its upper part said: We will not let you climb up and harm us. So those in its lower part said: We will pierce it from its bottom and draw water. He said: If they seize their hands and prevent them, they all survive, and if they leave them, they all drown."
"18552","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Musa, meaning Ibn Muslim al-Tahhan, narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abdullah, from his father or from his brother, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Those who mention the majesty of Allah, His glorification, His praise, His takbir, and His tahlil, they cluster around the Throne, having a humming like the humming of bees, reminding of their companion. Does not one of you love that there remains for him with Allah something that reminds of him."
"18553","Ya'la narrated to us, Abu Hayyan informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: My mother asked my father for some gift for me, so he granted it to me, then she said: I will not be satisfied until you call the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to witness. He said: My father took me by my hand, while I was a boy, and came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, the mother of this one, the daughter of Rawahah, pressed me for some gift for him, and I have granted it to him, and it pleased her that I call you to witness. He said: O Bashir, do you have another son besides this one. He said: Yes. He said: He said: Did you grant him the like of what you granted this one. He said: No. He said: Then do not call me to witness, for I do not bear witness to injustice."
"18554","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, Simak ibn Harb narrated to me, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Allah Almighty and His angels send blessings upon the first row, or the first rows."
"18555","Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he went out and would pray two rak'ahs and supplicate, and pray two rak'ahs and supplicate, until it cleared. He said: Some men claim that when the sun and moon eclipse, if one of them eclipses, it only eclipses for the death of a great one among the great, and it is not so, but they are two creations among the creation of Allah Almighty, so when Allah Almighty manifests Himself to something of His creation, it humbles itself to Him."
"18556","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Dawud, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: My father Bashir ibn Sa'd carried me to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, bear witness that I have granted al-Nu'man such-and-such, something he named. He said: He said: Did you grant all your children the like of what you granted al-Nu'man. He said: No. He said: Call someone else to witness. Then he said: Does it not please you that they be equal toward you in kindness. He said: Yes indeed. He said: Then not so."
"18557","Abdullah said: I found in the book of my father in his handwriting: Al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' Abu Tawbah, meaning al-Halabi, wrote to me, and in his letter was: Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from his brother Zayd ibn Sallam, that he heard Abu Sallam say: Al-Nu'man ibn Bashir narrated to me, he said: I was beside the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then a man said: I do not care if I do no deed after Islam except giving drink to the pilgrims. Another said: I do not care if I do no deed after Islam except maintaining the Sacred Mosque. Another said: Striving in the path of Allah is better than what you said. Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, rebuked them and said: Do not raise your voices at the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while it is Friday, but when I have prayed Friday, I will enter and ask him for a ruling about what you differed in. Then Allah sent down: Do you make giving drink to the pilgrims and maintaining the Sacred Mosque like one who believes in Allah and the Last Day, to the end of the whole verse."
"18558","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Mujalid, Amir narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he pointed with his two fingers to his ears: The lawful is clear, the unlawful is clear, and between the lawful and the unlawful are doubtful matters which many people do not know whether they are of the lawful or of the unlawful. Whoever leaves them clears himself for his religion and his honor, and whoever falls into them is likely to fall into the unlawful. Whoever pastures beside a sanctuary is likely to pasture in it. Every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah is His prohibitions."
"18559","He said: And I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir say: My father Bashir granted me a gift, then my mother said: Call the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to witness it. So he took me by my hand and went with me until we came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, the mother of this boy asked me to grant him a gift, so I granted it to him, and she said: Call the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to witness it, so I came to you to call you to witness. He said: Wait, do you have another child besides him. He said: Yes. He said: Did you give all of them as you gave him. He said: No. He said: Then do not call me to witness, I do not bear witness to injustice. Your sons have a right upon you that you be just among them."
"18560","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Zakariyya, he said: Amir narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir delivering a sermon, saying, and he pointed with his finger to his ears: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The example of the one who upholds the limits of Allah and the one who falls into them, or the one who compromises in them, is like a people who boarded a ship, so some of them got its lower part, its roughest and worst, and some of them got its upper part. When those in its lower part sought water, they passed by those above them and harmed them, so they said: If we made a hole in our share and drew water from it and did not harm those above us. If they leave them to their affair, they all perish, and if they seize their hands, they all survive."
"18561","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The example of the one who upholds the limits of Allah. Then he mentioned it."
"18562","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, he said: I heard Amir say: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The example of the one who upholds the limits of Allah. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"18563","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Zakariyya, he said: Amir narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir delivering a sermon, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The example of the believers in their mutual love, compassion, and mercy is like the body: when something of it complains, the rest of the body responds with sleeplessness and fever."
"18564","And I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The lawful is clear, the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters which many people do not know. Whoever avoids doubtful matters clears himself for his religion and his honor, and whoever falls into them falls into the unlawful, like the shepherd pasturing around the sanctuary, likely to pasture in it. Indeed every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah is what He has forbidden. Indeed in man there is a piece of flesh: if it is sound, the whole body is sound, and if it is corrupt, the whole body is corrupt. Indeed it is the heart."
"18565","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, he said: I heard Amir say: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The example of the believers. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"18566","Waki' narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to straighten the rows as arrows or spears are straightened."
"18567","Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Bishr informed us, from Habib ibn Salim, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I am the most knowledgeable of people, or like the most knowledgeable of people, of the time of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for Isha. He used to pray it after the setting of the moon on the third night of the beginning of the month."
"18568","Hushaym narrated to us, Sayyar informed us, and Mughirah informed us, and Dawud informed us, from al-Sha'bi, and Isma'il ibn Salim and Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: My father granted me a gift. Isma'il ibn Salim said: Apart from the people, he granted him a slave boy. He said: My mother Amrah bint Rawahah said to him: Go to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and call him to witness. He said: He came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him, and said: I have granted my son al-Nu'man a gift, and Amrah asked me to call you to witness that. He said: Do you have another child besides him. He said: I said: Yes. He said: Did you give all of them the like of what you gave al-Nu'man. He said: No. Some of these narrators said: This is injustice. And some of them said: This is coercion. So call someone else to witness this. And Mughirah said in his hadith: Does it not please you that they be equal to you in kindness and gentleness. He said: Yes. He said: Call someone else to witness this. And Mujalid mentioned in his hadith: They have a right upon you that you be just among them, just as you have a right upon them that they be dutiful to you."
"18569","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The example of the one who upholds the limits of Allah Almighty, the one who pastures in them, and the one who compromises in them, is like a people who drew lots for a ship, so some of them got its upper part and some of them got its lower part, its roughest. When those in its lower part sought water, they passed by their companions and harmed them, so they said: If we made a hole in our share and drew water from it and did not pass by our companions and harm them. If they leave them to what they want, they perish, and if they seize their hands, they all survive."
"18570","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The example of the believers in their mutual love, compassion, and mercy is like the body: when a limb of it complains, the rest of the body responds with sleeplessness and fever."
"18571","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Damrah ibn Sa'id, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, that al-Dahhak ibn Qays asked al-Nu'man ibn Bashir: What did the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recite in Friday prayer along with Surat al-Jumu'ah. He said: Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming."
"18572","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Nu'man ibn Bashir and Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, they both informed him that they heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir say: My father granted me a slave boy, so I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to call him to witness, so he said: Did you grant all your children. He said: No. He said: Then return it."
"18573","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from his father, from Habib ibn Salim, from his father, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited in the two Eids: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming, and if Friday coincided, he recited them both together. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Habib ibn Salim heard it from al-Nu'man and was his scribe, and Sufyan errs in it, saying: Habib ibn Salim from his father, while he heard it from al-Nu'man."
"18574","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I memorized it from Abu Farwah first, then from Mujalid, he heard it from al-Sha'bi, saying: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and whenever I heard him say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I listened attentively and drew near, fearing I would not hear anyone say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Lawful is clear, unlawful is clear, and doubtful matters are between them. Whoever leaves what is doubtful to him of sin is even more likely to leave what is clear to him, and whoever ventures upon what he doubts is likely to fall into the unlawful. Every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah on earth is His disobedience, or he said: His prohibitions."
"18575","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to set straight the rows as spears or arrows are set straight."
"18576","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Dharr, from Yusay' al-Kindi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Supplication is worship. Then he recited: And your Lord said: Call upon Me, I will answer you. Indeed those who are too proud for My worship will enter Hell humbled. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Yusay' al-Kindi is Yusay' ibn Ma'dan."
"18577","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: Ibrahim narrated to me, from Habib ibn Salim, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to recite in the Friday prayer: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming, and the Eid and Friday would sometimes coincide, so he recited these two surahs."
"18578","Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Isa Musa al-Saghir, he said: Awn ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from his father or from his brother, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Those who mention the majesty of Allah, His glorification, His praise, and His tahlil, they cluster around the Throne, having a humming like the humming of bees, reminding of their companion. Does not one of you love that there remains for him with Allah something that reminds of him."
"18579","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, Amr ibn Murrah narrated to me, he said: I heard Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd say: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: You will straighten your rows, or Allah will cause discord among your faces."
"18580","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir delivering a sermon, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The lightest of the people of the Fire in punishment on the Day of Resurrection is a man in whose soles two sandals of fire are placed, from which his brain boils."
"18581","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Dharr, from Yusay', from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Supplication is worship. Then he recited: Call upon Me, I will answer you."
"18582","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Qilabah, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed at the eclipse of the sun like your prayer, bowing and prostrating."
"18583","Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Khaythamah, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The believers are like one man: if his head complains, all of him complains, and if his eye complains, all of him complains."
"18584","Waki' narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Iyzar ibn Hurayth, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: Abu Bakr came asking permission to see the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and heard A'ishah raising her voice to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he gave him permission and he entered and said: O daughter of Umm Ruman, and he reached for her: Do you raise your voice to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came between him and her. He said: When Abu Bakr left, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, began saying to her, seeking to please her: Do you not see that I have come between the man and you. He said: Then Abu Bakr came and asked permission, and found him laughing with her. He said: He gave him permission and he entered, so Abu Bakr said to him: O Messenger of Allah, include me in your peace as you included me in your war."
"18585","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abu Azib, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Everything has a mistake except the sword, and every mistake has compensation."
"18586","Yazid narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Abu Bishr, from Bashir ibn Thabit, from Habib ibn Salim, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I am indeed the most knowledgeable of people, or among the most knowledgeable of people, of the time of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for Isha. He used to pray it when the moon disappears on the third or fourth night."
"18587","Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah and Abu al-Ala informed us, from Qatadah, from Habib ibn Salim, he said: A man was brought to al-Nu'man ibn Bashir whose wife had made her slave girl lawful for him, so he said: I will surely judge in it with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: If she had made her lawful for him, I will surely flog him a hundred lashes, and if she had not made her lawful for him, I will surely stone him. He said: He found that she had made her lawful for him, so he flogged him a hundred."
"18588","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir delivering a sermon, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, delivering a sermon, saying: I warn you of the Fire, I warn you of the Fire, I warn you of the Fire, until if a man were in the market, he would hear him from this station of mine. He said: Until a cloak that was upon his shoulder fell at his feet."
"18589","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, that he heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I warn you of the Fire, I warn you of the Fire, until if a man were in the farthest part of the market, he would hear him, and the people of the market would hear his voice while he was upon the pulpit."
"18590","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Simak, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to straighten us in the rows until it was as if he aligned us with arrows, then when he wanted to say takbir, he saw a man with his chest protruding, so he said: You will straighten your rows, or Allah will cause discord among your faces."
"18591","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Simak, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The example of the fighter in the path of Allah is like the one fasting his day and standing his night, until he returns, whenever he returns."
"18592","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Ziyad Abu Talhah al-Anmari narrated to me, that he heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir say upon the pulpit of Hims: We stood with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the night of the twenty-third in the month of Ramadan until the first third of the night, then we stood with him on the night of the twenty-fifth until half the night, then he led us on the night of the twenty-seventh until we thought we would not attain success. He said: We used to call suhur success. As for us, we say the seventh night is the night of the twenty-seventh, and you say the seventh is the night of the twenty-third. Who is more correct, us or you."
"18593","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to me, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever grants a gift of silver or gold, or gives milk to drink, or guides through a strait, it is like freeing a slave."
"18594","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: We accompanied the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and heard him say: Before the Hour there are trials like pieces of the dark night: a man wakes in them a believer then evenings a disbeliever, and evenings a believer then wakes a disbeliever. Peoples sell their share for a small price of this world, or for the goods of this world. Al-Hasan said: By Allah, we have seen them, images without minds, bodies without understanding, moths of fire and flies of greed, going in the morning for two dirhams and returning in the evening for two dirhams. One of them sells his religion for the price of a goat."
"18595","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Habib ibn Salim, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: A woman came to al-Nu'man ibn Bashir and said: Her husband had intercourse with her slave girl. He said: I will judge in that with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: If you made her lawful for him, I will strike him a hundred lashes, and if you did not make her lawful for him, I will stone him."
"18596","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Ibrahim al-Wasiti narrated to me, Habib ibn Salim narrated to me, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: We were sitting in the mosque with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Bashir was a man who withheld his narration, then Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani came and said: O Bashir ibn Sa'd, do you remember the narration of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the rulers. Hudhayfah said: I remember his sermon best. So Abu Tha'labah sat, then Hudhayfah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Prophethood will be among you as long as Allah wills it to be, then He will raise it when He wills to raise it. Then there will be a caliphate upon the method of prophethood, and it will be as long as Allah wills it to be, then He will raise it when Allah wills to raise it. Then there will be biting kingship, and it will be as long as Allah wills it to be, then He will raise it when He wills to raise it. Then there will be tyrannical kingship, and it will be as long as Allah wills it to be, then He will raise it when He wills to raise it. Then there will be a caliphate upon the method of prophethood. Then he fell silent. Habib said: When Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz came, and Yazid ibn al-Nu'man ibn Bashir was among his companions, I wrote to him with this hadith reminding him of it, and said to him: I hope the Commander of the Believers, meaning Umar, comes after the biting and tyrannical kingship. My letter was brought to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, and he was pleased with it and admired it."
"18597","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Khalid ibn Kathir al-Hamdani, that he narrated to him that al-Sari ibn Isma'il al-Kufi narrated to him that al-Sha'bi narrated to him that he heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Part of wheat is wine, part of barley is wine, part of raisins is wine, part of dates is wine, and part of honey is wine. And I forbid every intoxicant."
"18598","Hasan and Bahz with the meaning said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: I think it is from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: A man traveled in a barren land, Hasan said in his hadith, meaning a desert, then he said: Under a tree, and with him was his mount, upon it his waterskin and his food, then he woke and did not see it, so he climbed an elevation and did not see it, then climbed an elevation and did not see it, then he turned, and there it was dragging its halter. He is not more joyful with it than Allah is with the repentance of His servant when he repents. Bahz said: His servant when he repents to Him. Bahz said: Hammad said: I think it is from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"18599","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from his father, from Habib ibn Salim, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to recite in the two Eids and Friday: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming, and they would sometimes coincide in one day, so he recited them both. Abu Awanah said: And two Eids would sometimes coincide in one day."
"18600","Sufyan narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Sha'bi say: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir say, while he was governor of Kufah: My father granted me a slave boy, so I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to call him to witness, so he said: Did you grant all your children. He said: No. He said: I do not bear witness to injustice."
"18601","Sufyan narrated to us from Mujalid from al-Shabi, who heard it from al-Numan ibn Bashir: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The parable of the flatterer and the one who falls into the limits of Allah - Sufyan once said: the one who stands within the limits of Allah - is the parable of three who boarded a ship, and one of them got its lowest, roughest and worst part, and he had to come and go, and it became burdensome upon him each time he passed, so he said: I will make a hole that will be easier for me and I will not have to come and go over them, so some of them said: he is only making a hole in his own share, and others said: No; if they seize his hand he will be saved and they will be saved, and if they leave him he will perish and they will perish."
"18602","Sufyan narrated to us from Mujalid, al-Shabi narrated to us, who heard it from al-Numan ibn Bashir: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and whenever I heard him say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I thought I would never hear anyone on the pulpit say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: Indeed in man there is a morsel of flesh; if it is sound and healthy the rest of the body is sound and healthy, and if it is diseased the rest of the body is diseased and corrupt; indeed it is the heart."
"18603","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah informed us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq say: I heard al-Numan ibn Bashir while he was delivering a sermon say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The lightest in punishment among the people of Hell on the Day of Resurrection will be a man under whose soles two embers are placed, his brain will boil from them."
"18604","Rawh and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from al-Ashath ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jarmi from Abu Qilabah from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani from al-Numan ibn Bashir that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah wrote a book two thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth, then sent down two verses from it with which He sealed Surah al-Baqarah, and they are not recited in a house for three nights without Satan coming near it; Affan said: then let it not be approached."
"18605","Affan and Surayj narrated to us, they said: Abu Awanah narrated to us from Abu Bishr from Bashir ibn Thabit from Habib ibn Salim from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: By Allah, I am the most knowledgeable of people about the time of this prayer, the latter Isha prayer; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray it at the setting of the moon on the third night."
"18606","Yunus and Surayj narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb from al-Numan ibn Bashir that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and Surayj said in his hadith: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: The parable of the believers is like the body; when part of it aches the rest of it responds."
"18607","Ismail ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Maqil ibn Munabbih narrated to us, Abd al-Samad, meaning Ibn Maqil, narrated to me, he said: I heard Wahb say: Al-Numan ibn Bashir narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mention al-Raqim, and he said: Three men were in a cave, and the mountain fell upon the mouth of the cave and it was closed upon them; one of them said: Remind one another which of you did a good deed, so that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, in His mercy may have mercy on us; a man among them said: I did a good deed once; I had hired workers, and my laborers came to me, and I hired each man among them for a known wage, then one day a man came to me in the middle of the day and I hired him for half of what his companions got, and he worked in the rest of his day as much as each man among them worked in his whole day, and I saw it binding upon me in duty not to reduce him from what I had hired his companions for, because of his striving in his work, so a man among them said: Do you give this one the same as you gave me, though he worked only half a day, so I said: O servant of Allah, I did not wrong you anything of your condition; it is only my wealth, I dispose of it as I wish; he said: So he grew angry and went away and left his wage; he said: So I placed his due in a corner of the house as long as Allah willed, then cattle passed by me after that, and I bought with it a young cow, and it grew as much as Allah willed, then after a while an old weak man passed by me whom I did not know, and he said: I have a right with you, and he reminded me of it until I recognized him, so I said: It is you I seek; this is your right, and I offered it all to him, so he said: O servant of Allah, do not mock me; if you will not give charity to me, give me my right; he said: By Allah, I am not mocking you; it is indeed your right, I have nothing of it, so I handed it all over to him; O Allah, if I did that for Your sake, relieve us; he said: So the mountain split until they saw through it and could see; the other said: I did a good deed once; I had surplus, and hardship befell the people, and a woman came to me seeking a favor from me; he said: So I said: By Allah, it is not without yourself; she refused me and went away, then she returned and reminded me by Allah, but I refused her and said: No, by Allah, it is not without yourself, so she refused me and went away, and she mentioned it to her husband, so he said to her: Give him yourself and enrich your dependents, so she returned to me and adjured me by Allah, but I refused her and said: By Allah, it is not without yourself, and when she saw that she yielded herself to me, and when I uncovered her and was about to have her she trembled beneath me, so I said to her: What is the matter with you, she said: I fear Allah, Lord of the worlds; I said to her: You feared Him in hardship, and I did not fear Him in ease, so I left her and gave her what was due upon me for having uncovered her; O Allah, if I did that for Your sake, relieve us; he said: So it split until they recognized and it became clear to them; the other said: I did a good deed once; I had two old aged parents, and I had sheep, and I used to feed my parents and give them drink, then I returned to my sheep; he said: One day rain befell me and detained me, and I did not leave until evening came, then I came to my family and took my milking vessel and milked while my sheep were standing, then I went to my parents and found them asleep, and it was hard upon me to wake them and hard upon me to leave my sheep, so I remained sitting with my milking vessel in my hand until morning woke them, then I gave them drink; O Allah, if I did that for Your sake, relieve us; Al-Numan said: As if I hear this from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The mountain burst open, so Allah relieved them and they came out."
"18608","Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Farwah from al-Shabi from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters; whoever leaves what is doubtful to him of sin or of the matter, he is more avoiding of what is clear to him, and whoever ventures upon what he doubts is about to fall into what is clear, and whoever grazes around the sanctuary is about to fall into it."
"18609","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us from Hajib ibn al-Mufaddal, meaning Ibn al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufrah, from his father from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be just among your children."
"18610","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Al-Qawariri and al-Muqaddami narrated to me, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Hajib ibn al-Mufaddal, meaning Ibn al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufrah, from his father from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be just among your children."
"18611","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, al-Iyzar ibn Hurayth narrated to us, he said: Al-Numan ibn Bashir said, he said: Abu Bakr sought permission upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he heard the voice of Aishah raised, and she was saying: By Allah, I knew that Ali is more beloved to you than my father and than me, two or three times; then Abu Bakr sought permission and entered and rushed toward her, and he said: O daughter of so-and-so, shall I hear you raising your voice upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"18612","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Hajib ibn al-Mufaddal ibn al-Muhallab from his father, he said: I heard al-Numan ibn Bashir delivering a sermon, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be just among your children, be just among your children."
"18613","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik, meaning al-Harrani, narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us from Simak from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Allah, Allah is more joyful at the repentance of His servant than a man who was on a journey in a desert land, and he betook himself to the shade of a tree and slept beneath it, then woke and did not find his mount, then he came to an elevation and climbed it and looked and saw nothing, then he came to another and looked and saw nothing, then he said: I will return to my place where I was and remain in it until I die; he said: So he went, and there was his mount dragging its rein; he said: So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is more joyful at the repentance of His servant than this man with his mount."
"18614","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Jabir narrated to us, Abu Azib narrated to us, he said: We visited al-Numan ibn Bashir concerning a testimony, and I heard him say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said - or I heard him say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Everything accidental is a mistake except the sword, and in every mistake there is blood-money."
"18615","Bahz narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid, and he is al-Attar, narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Urfutah narrated to me from Habib ibn Salim from al-Numan ibn Bashir that a man called Abd al-Rahman ibn Hunayn, who was nicknamed Qurqur, fell upon the slave-girl of his wife; he said: So he was brought to al-Numan ibn Bashir al-Ansari, and he said: I shall surely judge concerning you with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: if she made her lawful to you I shall flog you a hundred, and if she did not make her lawful to you I shall stone you with stones; he said: And she had made her lawful to him, so he flogged him a hundred."
"18616","And he said: I heard Aban say: And Qatadah informed us that he wrote concerning it to Habib ibn Salim, and he wrote to him with this."
"18617","Affan narrated to us, Aban al-Attar narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from Khalid ibn Urfutah from Habib ibn Salim - and Aban said: Qatadah informed us that he wrote to Habib ibn Salim concerning it, and he wrote to him - that a man called Abd al-Rahman ibn Hunayn, who was nicknamed Qurqur, was brought to al-Numan ibn Bashir, having had intercourse with the slave-girl of his wife, and he said: I shall surely judge concerning you with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: if she made her lawful to you I shall flog you a hundred, and if she did not make her lawful to you I shall stone you; so he found that she had made her lawful to him, and he flogged him a hundred."
"18618","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb informed us from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to straighten us in the rows as arrows are straightened, until when he thought that we had learned that from him and understood it, he turned one day with his face, and there was a man standing apart with his chest, so he said: You shall surely straighten your rows, or Allah will surely set your faces apart."
"18619","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us from Zaidah from Asim from Khaythamah from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of people is my generation in which I am, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then there will come a people whose testimony will precede their oaths and whose oaths will precede their testimony."
"18620","Waki narrated to us from Ismail from al-Shabi, and Zakariya from al-Shabi from Abdullah ibn Utbah, and Fitr from Abu al-Duha from al-Numan ibn Bashir that Bashir came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wanting to grant al-Numan a gift; he said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you have any other child besides him, he said: Yes, he said: Did you give all of them what you gave him, he said: No; Fitr said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Like this - meaning: make them equal - and Zakariya and Ismail said: I do not bear witness to injustice."
"18621","Waki narrated to us, Zakariya narrated to us from Abu al-Qasim al-Jadali - my father said: and Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Zakariya informed us from Husayn ibn al-Harith Abu al-Qasim - that he heard al-Numan ibn Bashir say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned with his face to the people and said: Straighten your rows, three times; by Allah, you shall surely straighten your rows, or Allah will surely set your hearts apart; he said: So I saw a man join his ankle to the ankle of his companion, and his knee to his knee, and his shoulder to his shoulder."
"18622","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from Misar - he said: and Abd al-Razzaq said: Sufyan informed us - from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir from his father from Habib ibn Salim from al-Numan ibn Bashir that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to recite in the two Eids and Jumuah: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Has there come to you the story of the Overwhelming."
"18623","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Dharr al-Hamdani from Yusay from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Supplication is worship; then he recited: And your Lord said: Call upon Me, I will answer you."
"18624","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from al-Shabi from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The believers are like one man; when his head complains the rest of the body responds with fever and sleeplessness."
"18625","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, he said: Khaythamah from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The believers are like one man; when his head complains all of it complains, and if his eye complains all of it complains."
"18626","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from Simak from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in prayer, and he saw a man with his chest out of the row, so he said: Be straight, and do not differ, lest your hearts differ."
"18627","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Mansur and al-Amash from Dharr from Yusay al-Hadrami from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, delivering a sermon and saying: Supplication is worship; then he recited: And your Lord said: Call upon Me, I will answer you."
"18628","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Mansur from Dharr from Yusay al-Hadrami from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, and he mentioned the like; thus Shubah said the like; Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I was told that Usay is Yusay ibn Madan al-Hadrami."
"18629","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us from Damrah ibn Said from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah that al-Dahhak ibn Qays asked al-Numan ibn Bashir: What did the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recite in Jumuah along with Surah al-Jumuah, he said: Has there come to you the story of the Overwhelming."
"18630","Ismail narrated to us from Yunus from al-Hasan that al-Numan ibn Bashir wrote to Qays ibn al-Haytham: You are our brothers and our full brothers; we witnessed and you did not witness, and we heard and you did not hear; and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: Before the Hour there are tribulations like pieces of the dark night; a man will be a believer in them in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, and peoples will sell their share for a gain of this world."
"18631","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Salim ibn Abi al-Jad say: I heard al-Numan ibn Bashir say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: You shall surely straighten your rows in your prayer, or Allah will surely set your faces apart."
"18632","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard al-Numan ibn Bashir say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to straighten the row until he made it like a spear or an arrow; he said: Then he saw the chest of a man protruding, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O servants of Allah, you shall surely straighten your rows, or Allah will surely set your faces apart."
"18633","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hashim narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir from his father - Hashim said, meaning in his hadith: I heard my father narrate - from Habib ibn Salim from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to recite in Jumuah - Hashim said: in the Jumuah prayer on Friday - Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Has there come to you the story of the Overwhelming, and when two Eids coincided he would recite them both."
"18634","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us - and Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us - from Asim al-Ahwal from Abu Qilabah from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he prayed; and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would bow and prostrate; Hajjaj said: like our prayer."
"18635","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Abu Bishr from Khalid ibn Urfutah from Habib ibn Salim from al-Numan ibn Bashir from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said concerning the man who approaches the slave-girl of his wife, he said: If she made her lawful to him I would flog him a hundred, and if she did not make her lawful to him I would stone him."
"18636","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Said narrated to us from Qatadah from Habib ibn Salim - Ibn Bakr said: the freedman of al-Numan ibn Bashir - from al-Numan ibn Bashir that a man who had intercourse with the slave-girl of his wife was brought to him, and he said: I shall surely judge concerning her with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: if she made her lawful to you I shall flog you a hundred lashes, and if she did not make her lawful to you I shall stone you; he said: So he found that she had made her lawful to him, and he flogged him a hundred."
"18637","Hushaym narrated to us from Abu Bishr from Habib ibn Salim from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: A woman came to him and said: Her husband had intercourse with her slave-girl; he said: Indeed I have a decisive report about that taken from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: if you permitted him I shall strike him a hundred, and if you did not permit him I shall stone him; he said: So the people turned to her and said: Your husband will be stoned; say that you had permitted him; so she said: I had permitted him, so he brought him forward and struck him a hundred."
"18638","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr informed us from Asim from Khaythamah from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of people is my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then a people whose testimony will precede their oaths and whose oaths will precede their testimony."
"18639","Muawiyah ibn Abdullah ibn Muawiyah ibn Asim ibn al-Mundhir ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Sallam Abu al-Mundhir al-Qari narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us from al-Shabi or Khaythamah from al-Numan, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The parable of the Muslims is only like one man; when part of him aches the rest of his body responds."
"18640","Abdullah narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Abu Waki al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us from Abu Abd al-Rahman from al-Shabi from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said upon the pulpit: Whoever does not thank the little does not thank the much, and whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah; speaking of the blessing of Allah is gratitude, and abandoning it is ingratitude; unity is mercy, and division is punishment."
"18641","Abdullah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Abu Waki narrated to us from Abu Abd al-Rahman from al-Shabi from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said upon these pieces of wood, or upon this pulpit: Whoever does not thank the little does not thank the much, and whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah; and speaking of the blessing of Allah is gratitude, and abandoning it is ingratitude; and unity is mercy, and division is punishment; he said: So Abu Umamah al-Bahili said: Hold to the greatest multitude; he said: So a man said: What is the greatest multitude, so Abu Umamah said: This verse in Surah al-Nur: If they turn away, upon him is only what he was charged with, and upon you is what you were charged with."
"18642","Abdullah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, Hajib ibn al-Mufaddal, meaning Ibn al-Muhallab, narrated to us from his father from al-Numan ibn Bashir that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Treat your children fairly, meaning: make them equal."
"18643","Abdullah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Bahili and Ubaydullah al-Qawariri and Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Hajib ibn al-Mufaddal ibn al-Muhallab from his father that he heard al-Numan ibn Bashir say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be just among your children, be just among your children, be just among your children."
